                                "sense_id": "6698052f-15f4-3c63-8cd5-461a0bc3f117",
                                "text": "...Hastily arranging her necessities, her wishes, her fears, and her desires, she thus began to address the dear friend she alike dreaded, despised, and persevered in attaching to herself and her measures:—\n\"Bring any one you deem a desirable parti, of course, but allow me to observe, dear Lady Penrhyn, that——\"\n\"Yes! I see, that they must be really crême a la crême...."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65fd89c4-2527-4c68-85d9-e3aee26b36d8",
                                "sense_id": "6698052f-15f4-3c63-8cd5-461a0bc3f117",
                                "text": "We met some time ago a man that would just do for you, if you were not already engaged to Jonathan. He is an excellent parti, being handsome, well off, and of good birth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32081251-b98b-4658-9f4a-fd7db2e7c408",
                                "sense_id": "6698052f-15f4-3c63-8cd5-461a0bc3f117",
                                "text": "“My temper is sweet, and my character without blemish. In fine, Miss Dobson, I am a most desirable parti.”"
                            }
                        ]
